{
  "assembly_notes": "Pull-out (sleeper) sofa bed. One rigid sofa_frame root carries the upholstered carcass, the fixed arms, the apron and the carriage guides; a fixed seat_deck is the rear bed section. The backrest is a REVOLUTE (+x) child of the frame. The pullout_deck is a PRISMATIC (+y) child of the frame running in the guides. Two mattress_leaf panels ride the carriage: leaf 0 is a REVOLUTE (-x) child of the deck and leaf 1 a REVOLUTE (-x) child of leaf 0, so they fold up and back over the carriage rather than down through the seat. bed_leg_count fold-down bed_leg supports are REVOLUTE (+x) children of leaf 1. Every leaf plane sits a clearance above the seat cushion top, so a leaf laid flat while the carriage is retracted passes over the seat instead of into it, and every single-joint pose is genuinely clear. Four component slots vary without touching the mechanism: back_style, deck_frame, mattress_build and bed_leg. width_m, seat_depth_m and bed_height_m are independent continuous parameters deriving leaf length, carriage travel, hinge heights, leg length and rail spacing; palette and tufting counts are non-core.",
